within  that latent variable space that's task  relevant even when that's distributed  across neurons particularly this is  important when the information is  distributed across neurons so we can  find what patterns of collective  behavior collective activity are  responsible for producing that behavior  so that's what i have for you today and  i want to thank all the amazing  scientists who contributed to this  effort uh the inverse rational control  stuff was led by  wu and minhei kwan uh with major  contributions from sarab dr  and this has been a very beautiful  collaboration with paul schrader  for a good period of time and we have a  bunch of experimental collaborators who  have been working on these same tasks  with us and i hope to report soon on  some of the data that we're getting from  their lab and our analyses of it  the neural coding stuff was done by raj  kumar raju and julie  as well as a bunch of other  collaborators that we're trying to apply  that work on and so thank you for your  attention thank you to the funding  agencies who made all this work possible  and if you're interested in applying any  of these frameworks to your stuff  give me a contact give me a call or drop  me a line xaq rice.edu is my email and i  hope to hear from you and i look forward  to the upcoming debate  you
 

